{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-colossians-004",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 4,
  "title": "Colossians 4",
  "display_title": "Colossians 4",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "colossians",
  "book": "Colossians",
  "bookName": "Colossians",
  "bookOrder": 51,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 4,
  "sortOrder": 51004,
  "verseCount": 18,
  "aliases": [
    "Col",
    "Co"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Masters, give unto your servants that which is just and equal; knowing that ye also have a Master in heaven.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Continue in prayer, and watch in the same with thanksgiving;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Withal praying also for us, that God would open unto us a door of utterance, to speak the mystery of Christ, for which I am also in bonds:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "That I may make it manifest, as I ought to speak.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Walk in wisdom toward them that are without, redeeming the time.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Let your speech be alway with grace, seasoned with salt, that ye may know how ye ought to answer every man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "All my state shall Tychicus declare unto you, who is a beloved brother, and a faithful minister and fellowservant in the Lord:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Whom I have sent unto you for the same purpose, that he might know your estate, and comfort your hearts;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "With Onesimus, a faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They shall make known unto you all things which are done here.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Aristarchus my fellowprisoner saluteth you, and Marcus, sister’s son to Barnabas, (touching whom ye received commandments: if he come unto you, receive him;)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And Jesus, which is called Justus, who are of the circumcision. These only are my fellowworkers unto the kingdom of God, which have been a comfort unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Epaphras, who is one of you, a servant of Christ, saluteth you, always labouring fervently for you in prayers, that ye may stand perfect and complete in all the will of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "For I bear him record, that he hath a great zeal for you, and them that are in Laodicea, and them in Hierapolis.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas, greet you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Salute the brethren which are in Laodicea, and Nymphas, and the church which is in his house.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And when this epistle is read among you, cause that it be read also in the church of the Laodiceans; and that ye likewise read the epistle from Laodicea.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And say to Archippus, Take heed to the ministry which thou hast received in the Lord, that thou fulfil it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:colossians:4:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "The salutation by the hand of me Paul. Remember my bonds. Grace be with you. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Colossians 4:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:colossians:4:18"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
